# Veyvio Production Readiness Blueprint v1

**Canonical file:** [`docs/plan/veyvio-production-readiness-blueprint.md`](docs/plan/veyvio-production-readiness-blueprint.md)

This is the **engineering execution authority** for production stabilisation. Combined Blueprint v2.0 remains product authority. Where sequence or freeze conflict with older plan trackers, this programme wins until `VEYVIO-PROD` closes.

## Freeze (until VEYVIO-PROD closes)

Allowed: bug fixes, security fixes, production-readiness, tests, release engineering, necessary operational fixes.

Blocked: new major modules, large redesigns, custom-service architecture, large navigation changes, new transport product areas, non-critical refactors.

Do **not** rebuild Driver, Command, Yard, RLS, entitlements, Wave 3F tooling, F-03, or CI from scratch. Improve and close them.

Wave 3G (`organisation_id`) starts only after Wave 3F is LOCKED. Do not mix tenancy redesign into production stabilisation.

## Permanent architecture

Ordinary tenant CRUD: authenticated request → `UserScopedDb` → RLS → tenant data.

Privileged work only via named capabilities (`authAdmin`, `storageSigner`, `billingAdmin`, `platformAdmin`). Generic `admin.from(...)` in production modules is a CI failure.

Unavailable real data must never become believable fake operational data (F-03).

`main` + immutable release SHA define production. Released migrations are never edited.

## Execution order

Start at **PROD-0 / PROD-1**, not SaaS or mobile.

Critical path: repository authority → Wave 3F + production truth → relational integrity → reproducible CI/DB → release candidate → (SaaS / mobile / reliability) → controlled pilot.

Map work to tracks **PR-00–PR-12**. Every P0 needs an owner. Do not convert remaining privileged modules in one PR — batch and prove the security matrix each time.

## Release evidence

No percentage-ready claims. Dashboard counts and PASS/FAIL only. Gate A (pilot) before Gate B (first paying customer) before Gate C (GA).
